practiceProblems.description:
A developer placed a print statement before `this(...)`, causing a compilation error:

```java
Member(String name) {
    System.out.println("Creating member"); // ❌ Error!
    this(name, "Standard");
}
```

Fix the error by making `this(name, "Standard");` the very first statement.
In `Main`, create `Member m = new Member("Pooja");` and verify it prints: `Creating member
Member: Pooja (Standard)`.

