practiceProblems.description:
Examine this circular constructor deadlock:

```java
class Widget {
    Widget() { this(10); }
    Widget(int x) { this(); } // ❌ Recursive call deadlock!
}
```

Fix it by letting `Widget(int x)` be the master constructor that actually sets `this.x = x;`.
In `Main`, create `Widget w = new Widget();` and print: `Widget value: 10`.

